From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: zenbook-a16: describe the EC, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and board supplies

Adds the ASUS Zenbook A16 (UX3607OA) embedded controller driver and its
binding, and completes the A16 device tree: the EC, the QCC2072 Wi-Fi and
its Bluetooth on a WCN7850 power sequencer, the eDP supplies held on
(dropping them on panel power-down resets the SoC), both Type-C
controllers in host mode, the RTC without the UEFI offset this firmware
cannot provide, SCMI polling (without it cpufreq never probes), and
passive cooling maps for every CPU and LLC zone.

The EC driver is Konrad Dybcio's, as Linux 7.4 carries it, without the
keyboard backlight that hid-asus registers for this keyboard.
---
